---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlaceholderImage from '../components/PlaceholderImage.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';

import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="How a corporate career turned into a ceramics practice, and why that led to wanting to teach."
  active="about"
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-4 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">About</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-10 sm:px-8">
    <div class="grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-5 sm:gap-14">
      <div class="sm:col-span-3">
        <p class="max-w-measure leading-relaxed text-clay">
          I came to ceramics somewhat accidentally. I didn't go to art school and didn't grow up thinking of myself as particularly artistic. 
          I started taking pottery classes after college while working a corporate job and, for quite a while, I was pretty bad at it.
          But I loved it enough to keep going. Over the last five years, 
          I've practiced in community studios in San Francisco, Boston, and New York, taking classes along the way and spending a lot of hours at the wheel. 
          Ceramics has become the rare thing that can completely hold my attention while also giving me endless room to experiment
          Kristin and the Machine is the name I've given to all of that—the things I make, the things that don't work, and my ongoing relationship with the pottery wheel.
        </p>
      </div>
      <img
        src="/images/koi-fish-about.png"
        alt="koi fish mug"
        class="aspect-[3/4] w-full object-cover sm:col-span-2"
      />
    </div>
    
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
